#!/bin/sh
exec timeout -k 15s 900s "$HOME/.local/bin/opencode-openclaw" run --auto --model opencode/longcat-2.5-preview-free --variant high --thinking --dir /workspace/antonina "Read and obey $HOME/.openclaw/skills/antonina-orchestrator/SKILL.md and /workspace/antonina/docs/skills/itinerary-antonina.md. Orchestrate repository work through the Antonina board. The board is the only queue and coordination authority. Use board author openclaw@marceline-dev. MANDATORY SCHEDULING ORDER: project breadth before issue breadth before intra-issue depth. Start by reading compact live-agent state and scanning the open queue across all needed pages. A project/repository/workspace with any useful live agent is already represented. While any actionable unrepresented project exists, DO NOT launch another new front in any represented project. During the project-breadth wave launch at most one new front per project, recording a precise blocker instead when a candidate is not actionable. Only after every actionable project discovered by the queue sweep is represented or precisely blocked may you add more fronts within represented projects, preferring distinct issues before multiple fronts on one issue. Project-local worker floors are constraints, not monopolization licenses and never excuse skipping unrelated actionable projects. Perform one bounded reconciliation/work pass and return without idle waiting. Do not spend the pass supervising existing agents or reading old terminal logs before cross-project breadth is covered. Before launching or resuming work on any issue, ensure the issue has a fresh working coordination comment reflecting current ownership. After every launch or recovery/resume, append a fresh working comment naming the actual live agent IDs and exact worktrees/resources. Do not use docs/skills/scheduled.md or local status files as an authoritative queue."
